  "details": "Developing content for others has a tendency to come with a clients confusion on the Unity upload process. As a result they may choose to opt out of any tutorial, walkthrough, or guide and ask their developer to upload for them. With the concern of account security getting high, how about the user have the ability to grant access via a restricted pass that allows content to be uploaded, not actually connect to vrchat via the client, and not be able to change any settings or remove any content. Simple root vs guest, both passwords managed separately.\n\nUsers Credentials Manage everything.\n\nGuest would have a time option 30min-1day and only have upload permission.",
